commit f74a57400ace5006ab75504c64df89c7cd78ff3d
Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 20 07:33:43 2026 -0800

    Windows: quitting no longer crashes when error reports are on

    JusPrin 2.0.1 stopped Sentry from an atexit handler. On Windows that runs
    while OrcaSlicer.dll is being unloaded, and Sentry's last upload starts a
    thread there. Starting it throws std::system_error, nothing catches it, and
    the app aborts with 0x40000015 (Sentry issue JUSPRIN-APP-2).

    Sentry now stops at the end of GUI_App::OnExit, after the windows close and
    while threads can still start.

    On a Windows VM, 2.0.1 crashed on 8 of 8 quits with reports on and exited
    cleanly with them off. 2.0.1 with this change exited cleanly on 8 of 8, and
    a stand-in Sentry server received the final "session exited" report at quit
    instead of a crash dump.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7WSF5BJR446PF75A86EHNNJ

